Changed file: internal/analyzerswift/parser.go

Intent:
analyzerswift: admit attributes and report the real refusal reason

The Swift candidate parsed 10.7% of beamfall-apple's 391 first-party Swift
files, and 87.2% of the corpus reported DYNAMIC_INPUT -- a code that sent
coverage triage looking for interpolation that was almost never the cause.

Reason codes now name the actual cause. DYNAMIC_INPUT is reserved for bytes
whose meaning depends on a value absent from the input: string interpolation
in plain, multiline, and raw literals. Conditional compilation and
freestanding macros/pound literals are real Swift outside the closed matrix
and report UNSUPPORTED_SCHEMA. A body over the source ceiling is a
bounded-resource refusal and reports LIMIT_EXCEEDED, not MALFORMED_INPUT.

Attributes are admitted in one closed form -- `@` plus an identifier,
optionally followed by one balanced parenthesised argument clause with no
brace -- before a declaration or import and before each inherited type. An
attribute carries no tuple under ACP-004's frozen fact matrix, so it is
consumed as part of the declaration it decorates and contributes no fact; an
attribute run not followed by a declaration or import still rejects.

Measured white-box over the same corpora, binding gate bypassed:
beamfall-apple 42/391 (10.7%) -> 77/391 (19.7%); beamfall-apple-ui 38/207
(18.4%) -> 90/207 (43.5%). Conditional compilation is the dominant remaining
refusal and stays rejected: its declaration set depends on a configuration
absent from the input, which ACP-004 and SAC-004 require failing.

The rejection table now pins the exact reason for every refused construct in
both directions, replacing one that asserted only "some reason" and so could
not see a wrong code. TestTokenOffsetsHoldAtMaximalSource asserts the
one-byte margin between the uint16 token offsets and maxSourceSize, so
raising the ceiling without widening the offsets fails there rather than
wrapping a start offset into a valid-looking slice of the wrong bytes.

ACP-009 closure 41,215/65,536 (headroom 24,321); no ceiling amendment.
BenchmarkAnalyzeCandidate 52,443 B/op / 105 allocs (base 52,502 / 105).

